m Viewbook\nCurrent Students\nCurrent Students\nCurrent Students\nNewly Admitted\nNewly Admitted\nNewly Admitted\nGraduate Student Orientation Portal\nRegistration\nRegistration\nRegistration\nAnnual Registration\nConcurrent Registration\nConfirmation of registration\nCourse registration\nRegistration status\nStudying at another university\nHow to use your Student Centre (including updating personal information)\nThesis-based students\nThesis-based students\nThesis-based students\nAcademic Schedule\nFees and funding\nGraduate Awards Database\nSupervision\nThesis\nAnnual Progress Report (APR)\nExams\nImportant Resources and Supports\nGraduation and Convocation\nStudent Appeals\nCourse-based students\nCourse-based students\nCourse-based students\nAcademic Schedule\nFees and funding\nGraduate Awards Database\nManaging grad school\nTerm-Based Registration\nAcademic Integrity\nImportant Resources and Supports\nStudent Appeals\nGraduation and Convocation\nIndigenous Graduate Students\nImportant resources and supports\nImportant resources and supports\nImportant resources and supports\nAcademic Calendar\nForms and documents\nGraduate AI Guidelines\nService Requests and eForms\nGraduate advising\nFind Graduate Program Staff\nWho to ask\nAwards and Funding\nAwards and Funding\nAwards and Funding\nAward Opportunities\nAward Opportunities\nAward Opportunities\nCanada Graduate Research Scholarships - Doctoral (CGRS D)\nGraduate Awards Database\nDoctoral Recruitment Scholarships\nApplying, Accepting and Managing Awards\nAward Policies and Regulations\nFunding Thesis-based Students\nExceptional scholars\nContact the Awards Office\nProfessional Development\nProfessional Development\nProfessional Development\nCommunication Skills and Competitions\nCommunication Skills and Competitions\nCommunication Skills and Competitions\nThree Minute Thesis\nThree Minute Thesis\nThree Minute Thesis\n2026 3MT Finalists\n2026 3MT Finals' Hosts and Judges\nPast Three Minute Thesis Videos\nImages of Research\nResearch communication skills\nWIL and Internships\nOn Campus Resources\nSupervisory Resources\nSupervisory Resources\nSupervisory Resources\nBecoming a Supervisor\nMaintaining your supervisor profile\nSupervisory Renewal\nSupervisor responsibilities and resources\nGraduate oral examinations\nSupervisors and VSRs\nAcademic Calendar\nGRADnet SharePoint\nAbout Us\nAbout Us\nAbout Us\nThe Dean\nLeadership team\nFGS Council\nFGS Council\nFGS Council\nMembership\nCommittees of Council\nMinutes and meetings\nFGS Action Plan\nContacts\nFunding support for thesis-based students\nUCalgary is proud to be a top Canadian research university, committed to offering thesis\u2011based graduate students among the highest levels of funding in the U15.\nMinimum guaranteed funding\nThe University of Calgary provides some of the highest levels of funding for thesis-based graduate students in Canada. Full-time PhD students beginning their program on or after January 1, 2026, are guaranteed a minimum funding package of $31,426 for domestic students and $33,205 for international students. MA or MSc thesis-based students will receive a minimum funding package of $23,676 for domestic students and $25,455 for international students. These annual amounts are guaranteed for the first four years of a PhD program and the first two years of an MA or MSc thesis-based program.\nA student\u2019s guaranteed funding is contingent on continued full-time registration in their graduate program and maintaining satisfactory academic progress (as defined in G.H.3 Regulation).\nFunding packages\nStudent funding packages of individual graduate programs are designed to meet or exceed the university\u2019s minimum guaranteed levels. Program funding packages are typically composed of multiple sources, including stipends from supervisors\u2019 research grants, internal and external awards, and compensation for teaching or research assistantships. A student\u2019s funding offer letter will outline the minimum guaranteed amount, the sources of funding included or excluded, and how scholarships adjust the overall funding package, to place students in a strong financial position.\nApplying for awards\nGraduate students who have submitted their application and received their University of Calgary student number (UCID) should apply for internal and external awards and seek out Teaching Assistant and Research Assistant opportunities.\u202fStudents are not required to meet the eligibility requirements in the terms of reference of an award when they apply, but if successful, they must meet the eligibility requirements at the time the award is paid.\nLearn more about graduate award opportunities by visiting the Awards and Funding webpage.\nWebsite Terms & Conditions\nPrivacy Policy\nWebsite feedback\nUniversity of Calgary\n2500 University Drive NW\nCalgary Alberta T2N 1N4\nCANADA\nCopyright \u00a9 2026\nThe University of Calgary, located in the heart of Southern Alberta, both acknowledges and pays tribute\nto the traditional territories of the peoples of Treaty 7, which include the Blackfoot Confederacy\n(comprised of the Siksika, the Piikani, and the Kainai First Nations), the Tsuut\u2019ina First Nation,\nand the Stoney Nakoda (including Chiniki, Bearspaw, and Goodstoney First Nations). The city of Calgary\nis also home to the M\u00e9tis Nation within Alberta (including Nose Hill M\u00e9tis District 5 and Elbow M\u00e9tis\nDistrict 6).\nThe University of Calgary is situated on land Northwest of where the Bow River meets the Elbow River,\na site traditionally known as Moh\u2019kins\u2019tsis to the Blackfoot, W\u00eech\u00eespa to the Stoney Nakoda, and\nGuts\u2019ists\u2019i to the Tsuut\u2019ina. On this land and in this place we strive to learn together, walk\ntogether, and grow together \u201cin a good way.\u201d", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://grad.ucalgary.ca/awards-and-funding/funding-TB-students#content"], ["My UCalgary", "https://my.ucalgary.ca/"], [